                if token == 'z' and previous_word:
                    value += 10.0
            elif piece != 'az' or token[:1].isspace():
                value += 5.1
        if piece.endswith('zz'):
            value -= 3.3
        if piece.endswith('zi'):
            value += 4.1
        if piece.endswith('zion'):
            value += 2.5
        if piece.endswith('c'):
            value -= 1.4
        if piece.endswith('ci'):
            value -= 1.1
        if piece.endswith('ce'):
            value -= 0.9
        if piece.endswith('d'):
            value -= 0.6
    if token.lower() == 'i':
        value -= 0.3

    value *= italian
    if piece in ('ț', 'ţ'):
        value += 2.3
    return (doc, word, scores, cue_lifetime), float(value)

"""A spelling-based approximation to a mat/matic feature.

Predict negative responses to mat/matic pieces, including completions across
tokens and corresponding Cyrillic, Greek and Arabic letters. Common whole
words usually respond less strongly. Math library names and selected maz
pieces respond positively; escaped TeX math behaves differently.
State holds the unfinished word and recent import/include syntax. Amplitudes
are rounded training fits, not an exact account of context-dependent strength.
