"""Approximate a token-boundary fusion signal.

The main trigger is a token starting with punctuation (or a tab) glued
to a following letter. Slash/dot prefixes are especially negative;
length, case, and preceding whitespace adjust the response.
Ordinary tokens default to zero. Contractions/escapes, domain/file
suffixes, Chinese/Japanese grammatical prefixes, markup and document
starts have small rules. Some initial-token classes get positive values.
Spelling-specific variation within these surface classes is omitted.
