Closing punctuation is strongest for tightly attached expressions: function
arguments, subscripts and short quoted literals. Spacing at the last opener
separates these from prose parentheses and citations. Include headers, patch
hunks and here-document markers supply other boundary cues. A few literal
document-opening and control-character exceptions have much larger values.
